      "content": "That's good to hear. I noticed Reviewer 2 mentioned something about the p-value distributions looking a bit \"unnatural\" in the Monte Carlo simulations, and I was looking at the raw data too... it looks like they might have used a non-parametric test on data that clearly violates the underlying assumptions of the model they built. Doesn't that kind of stationarity issue potentially invalidate the whole 'breakthrough' claim they're making? \n\nWhat's your take on that specific point?",
